              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The rate of change of [B] can be expressed in terms of the rate of change of [A] using the stoichiometric coefficients: "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                    "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;=\\;-\\frac12\\frac{\\;\\triangle\\left[\\mathrm A\\right]}{\\triangle t}\\;=\\;+\\frac{\\triangle\\left[\\mathrm B\\right]}{\\triangle t}",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Using the average rate of change of [A] from Part 1 to calculate the average rate of change of [B]: "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                    "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;=\\;\\frac{\\triangle\\left[\\mathrm B\\right]}{\\triangle t}\\;=\\;-\\frac12\\frac{\\triangle\\left[\\mathrm A\\right]}{\\triangle t}\\; =\\;-\\frac12\\;(-0.015\\;\\mathrm M/\\mathrm s)\\;=\\;7.5\\;\\mathrm x\\;10^{-3}\\;\\mathrm{M/s}",
                    "subtype": "latex",
                    "type": "formula_inline"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " Note: Because B is a product, [B] increases and Δ[B]/Δ"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "t"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is positive. "
